# The binary is static (musl), one package per architecture for every
# Debian and Ubuntu release. The build needs a Rust toolchain (rustup) with
# the x86_64/aarch64-unknown-linux-musl targets and cargo-zigbuild (plus
# zig) on PATH; Debian's own rustc has no musl standard library.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/shinys000114/pkgpod
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/shinys000114/pkgpod
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/shinys000114/pkgpod.git

Package: pkgpod
Architecture: amd64 arm64
# ca-certificates: the HTTP client reads the system trust store; rsync:
# mirrors from rsync sources. Signing is done in process (no gpg).
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser, ca-certificates
Recommends: rsync
Description: package server for a team
 pkgpod hosts, mirrors and serves packages of 23 formats: Debian, RPM,
 Alpine, Arch and opkg repositories, OCI images, PyPI, npm, Cargo, Go,
 Maven, RubyGems, NuGet, Helm and more. Every hosted repository keeps
 its history: each change is a version, labels make snapshots that stay
 reachable at their own address, and any version can be compared with
 another or made current again. Debian, RPM, Alpine, Arch and opkg
 repositories publish signed indexes for every version.
 .
 Mirrors of Debian, RPM, Alpine and Arch repositories and of file trees
 follow their upstream on a schedule; proxies keep what clients fetch
 from public registries. Repositories are reached by their own host
 names and paths, and a host's root lists the repositories there.
 .
 One binary is the server (with a web console and a JSON API) and its
 command line client.
